{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f_{small, *} :\n\\Sh(X_\\etale)\n\\to\n\\Sh(Y_\\etale)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-property-C-implies}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:40e0b270e725dfec536996e96ba79909422731c9991fb20d69c8c72a555649e3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3ac395dfaf1ef6c00ac976d890f6299ce313ac602257eb7fc30299870ea572f6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Assume (C) holds. Then the functor\n<MATH_0002>\nreflects injections and surjections.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1dac221e84aef9492ac7dd85ad03a1c36660e1a6015fac17e505d82c6b03e111", "unit_id": "tag:04DT:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y_\\etale \\to X_\\etale$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\mapsto X \\times_Y V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-lemma-cover-from-below}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-cover-from-below}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:78e255be47af9357aefd5bab50fef682ddc5a7d7b2cb50ecdc5559855a62b3d9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48adf8e5df3336a322939882d9c57c562a727fb8a99d6e9ef25a7ede804e4916", "source_text": "Follows from\nSites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe omit the verification that property (C) implies that the functor\n<MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>\nsatisfies the assumption of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f862d9f63e7c99a7fb766f0333cd5d0f0bd5b2dbd0567c13463ebd977ea5e63f", "unit_id": "tag:04DT:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "04DS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\in \\Ob(X_\\etale)$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$Y_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\times_Y X = U$", "MATH_0006": "$f_{small, *}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-property-C-strong}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f76fe8200f316ab69b2c2db5a5a6852517dcba8e9fea736e42d43102bbf2f7e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4b29f9cc67a912b6d144597d59829a15acad2dc5955322b93f05e5ca1495896", "source_text": "Property (C) holds if <MATH_0001> is an open immersion. Namely, if\n<MATH_0002>, then we can view <MATH_0003> also as an object\nof <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>. Hence property (C)\ndoes not imply that <MATH_0006> is exact as this is not\nthe case for open immersions (in general).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ffe3a066a0c190939d2a7410d0ed776b0933b62143a2029cd19c433d2bd5a91a", "unit_id": "tag:04DU:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DS", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\times_Y V \\to V$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\times_Y V \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$Y_\\etale \\to X_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\mapsto X \\times_Y V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-almost-cocontinuous}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-property-C-closed-implies}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9ac26b8df8e5dfaa1f2731fe37765f9a8259e55a4921a91dd93b475835f4156f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7badf50874b640902f0d9865a204e3e2c661197f65a0a360ec93415f5a1e969e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Assume that\nfor any <MATH_0002> <ACCENT_0001>tale we have that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> has property (C), and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> is closed.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen the functor\n<MATH_0005>, <MATH_0006>\nis almost cocontinuous, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:41121e4e40d7cb3dffcf1173550663e7655e1c00fab7d1fcdbf1e14bd64c76fe", "unit_id": "tag:04DV:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DS", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Y_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U_i \\to X \\times_Y V\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "MATH_0006": "$h_i : V_i \\to V$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times_Y V_i \\to U_i$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\times_Y V$", "MATH_0009": "$\\bigcup h_i(V_i) \\subset V$", "MATH_0010": "$Z = \\Im(X \\times_Y V \\to V)$", "MATH_0011": "$h_0 : V_0 = V \\setminus Z \\to V$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}_{i \\in I \\cup \\{0\\}}$", "MATH_0013": "$i \\in I \\cup \\{0\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$V_i \\times_Y X = \\emptyset$", "MATH_0015": "$i = 0$", "MATH_0016": "$V_i \\times_Y X \\to V \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0017": "$U_i \\to X \\times_Y V$", "MATH_0018": "$i \\not = 0$", "MATH_0019": "$Y_\\etale \\to X_\\etale$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:04deb3e21ef7063ebb46b8b522d34eea20fd4a6128967ccea06ccf99e1faba56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c87a35c7dc5b15a758e0e981b3b585769968da4451baabd453709581314f491", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002> and let\n<MATH_0003> be a covering of <MATH_0004>.\nBy assumption (1) for each <MATH_0005> we can find an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0006> and a surjective morphism <MATH_0007>\nover <MATH_0008>. Note that <MATH_0009> is an\nopen set containing the closed set <MATH_0010>.\nLet <MATH_0011> be the open immersion.\nIt is clear that <MATH_0012> is an\n<ACCENT_0002>tale covering such that for each <MATH_0013> we have\neither <MATH_0014> (namely if <MATH_0015>), or\n<MATH_0016> factors through <MATH_0017>\n(if <MATH_0018>). Hence the functor <MATH_0019>\nis almost cocontinuous.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b42ee89436a7db95ef4f390f82962e2